<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n492" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăchĕrūsĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f.
		Acheruns. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Acherusia
			Palus, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A lake in Epirus</i>, <i>through which
				the Acheron flows</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 1,
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A lake in Campania</i>, <i>between
				Misenum and Cumae</i>, now <i>Lago di Fusaro</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 5, 9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A cave in Bithynia</i>, <i>from which
				Cerberus is said to have been dragged</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 19,
				7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 1, 1</span></i>; the same called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăchĕrūsĭs</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 5,
				73</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
